test_i2s_pair_blend_gate_bites:
  [gate 24e-b] 6/6 blend-binding mutations REJECTED
test_firmware_version_derived_from_rtl:
  [gate 24] firmware_version DERIVED from milan_csr VERSION 0x0002_0060 -> '2.96.0': 3/3 configs derive it and declare none, it lands zero-padded at ENTITY+116 in all 3 ROMs (1722.1 7.2.1 Table 7-2), no entity_model_id moves with it (6.2.2.8 exclusion; arty_current still pinned 0x001BC50AC1000006), firmware_rev 7 -> 2.96.7 with the same id, 4/4 bad declarations refused
test_d8_role_pools:
  [gate 24a] ax7101_8x8 role-pools: 72 AUDIO_CLUSTERs (8x empty-handed in, #259; 8x pilot1+loopback8 out), 0 physical because the board routes none, talker map -> pilot (fabric lane off), 8 distinct loopback sources offered
  [gate 24a] declaring routed channels re-introduces the physical pool AND moves the static map onto it (primary-role fallthrough): 8 routed channels, 123 writable names; 2/2 planted controls turned it red: 16 routed channels; no routed channel
  [gate 24a] the over-wide (72) D8 loopback pool (747 writable names) is REFUSED at generation by the saved-state NAME capacity, naming both figures, before any write; its own overlay's ROM exceeds the 16-bit AEM store address space (D6 is the owner), and behind a planted capacity it is marked rather than emitted and --write-rtl REFUSES it; 2/2 planted controls turned their check red: capacity 747; the shipped 8x8 overlay
  [gate 24a] #447 render lane: the declared width is bounded by the LANE and not the family, a shape with no render endpoint refuses a nonzero count, a TDM lane narrower than its own bus is refused with the full-bus-width rule, and every tracked config sits inside its own lane {'arty_current': ('i2s', 2, 0, 0), 'arty_4x4': ('i2s', 2, 0, 0), 'arty_8ch': ('i2s', 2, 0, 0), 'ax7101_8x8': ('tdm', 0, 2, 0), 'ax7101_1x1_tdm8': ('tdm', 8, 2, 8)}
